Z||000000||SilverFieroV6||05-09-2001||04:28 PM||||Ok i found a 86 v6 4spd for sale.  the lady who is selling it decided i can just have it for the cost of nothing.  i looked at the car it is excelent condition.  the car is a se  but the nose on the car isnt the normal nose piece for an se.  I was wondering if it might be a formula.  she said the car is completely stock  nothing has been changed since she bought it  (original owner).  There are also some small diferences ( im not sure if this is because its an 86 as i own an 85)  the tail pipes are a little larger, there are more speakers iin the car.  and there is another cluster with two different guages on top of the dash(right above the heater vents).<BR>Thanks for all the help<BR>Sam||||reg||5
Z||000001||Steve Normington||05-09-2001||04:42 PM||||AFAIK...<P>The nose on 85 SE's was the coupe nose (pointy with black bumper pads). The nose on 86 SE's was the GT nose, curved, no pads. I don't know about any changes to the size of the exhaust pipes. The speakers moved from the headrests to the panels. The cluster on top of the heater vents is the aux gage cluster which is part of the 120 mph speedo. Formulas were only available in 88. Also, 86 and later cars will have a third brake light.<P>Check out this sight for mor info: <A HREF="http://www.fiero.org/text/spotter.txt" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.org/text/spotter.txt</A> <P><P>------------------<BR>I don't car if my next Fiero is a 2M Hamster, I'm not swapping the engine.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Loki||05-09-2001||04:42 PM||||Hmmmmm...Starting in 86 they added the rear speakers to panels to the side panel trim (4x6") and removed the headrest speakers. Also in 86 they added the aux gauges to the console above heater controls...Ummm volts and oil pressure....As for the noce, what does it look like?<BR><P>------------------<BR>Loki<BR>ICQ# 16477998<BR>www.cox-internet.com/fiero  !!!UPDATED!!!||||reg||1
