Z||000013||mckay_lee||05-19-2001||02:06 AM||||Ok, now you got me wondering what my car is, they said it was an 86 SE when i bought it, but from what you say its not an 86 SE, So what is it. It has the third brake light, no aux gauge cluster, the coupe nose, the rear exhaust is two small pipes on the left, so whatis my car||||reg||5
Z||000014||maryjane||05-20-2001||12:41 AM||||Since you're on the subject of what year is what. I have an 84 se. I recently went to look at another 84Se(checked the date of manufactor on door). Mine has the eng vent grate in center of rear deck, the other had two vents-one each on either side of deck lid. Which is stock? only difference is mine is auto and the other is manual trans.Thanks<BR>Don||||reg||5
Z||000015||SilverFieroV6||05-20-2001||12:51 AM||||Hey don im kind of new to the fiero's and learning diferences (maybe someone will back me up on this)  but i belive that the stock 84 trunk has the vents in the center of the trunk.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.org/text/spotter.txt" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.org/text/spotter.txt</A> <P>this link might tell you someone sent it to me the other day it explains the differences in the certian year a fiero was made.<BR>Sam||||reg||1
Z||000016||Topknot||05-20-2001||07:34 AM||||Hallo mckay_lee,<P>Well don't know if it's any help, but the 86 SE I have that I am stripping down this weekend had all the items you mentioned except that I have the dual pipes out the rear.  It's an 86 SE 4cyl Automatic.  It came with the GT style nose, subwoofer with sliding switch located above in center front of roof, dual exaust out rear and auto windows.<P>I was also puzzled about what my car was but have come to stand that it was an 86 SE with a few extras in a sense.  But due to now getting an 86 GT 5 speed, it's become my new "hobbie" car and am stripping down the 86 to store some stuff in the garage and trash the rest, sad thought, would of liked to keep it since it ran and all.<P>Topknot =]<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000017||Steve Normington||05-20-2001||12:06 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by maryjane:<BR>Since you're on the subject of what year is what. I have an 84 se. I recently went to look at another 84Se(checked the date of manufactor on door). Mine has the eng vent grate in center of rear deck, the other had two vents-one each on either side of deck lid. Which is stock? only difference is mine is auto and the other is manual trans.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The date of manufacture may not be the model year. The VIN code will be able to tell you what model year it is. If the ninth digit is an 'E', then it is an 84; an 'F', 85. The center vent was only on 84's.<P>||||reg||1
